# Interfaces & code budgets

## Conditioning vector (live pack = **4** numbers, Phases 1–2)
Logged / trained layout (`CONDITIONING_LAYOUT`):
| Field | Dim | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `p_hat_x/y(t+Δ)` | 2 | Predicted object XY at action-landing time |
| `v_hat_x/y` | 2 | Object XY velocity |

**Δ is fixed** from `sim/phase0_cfg.yaml` → `state_machine_params.conditioning_delta_s`
(collect / train / eval must agree). It is **not** packed while it is constant.
Train noise comes from `policy/configs/smolvla_b.yaml`. Pack Δ as a 5th number
only when deploy latency genuinely varies (Phase 3 latency sweep / Phase 4 real arm).

With fixed Δ, clean `[p̂, v̂]` is an invertible transform of `[p, v]` — phrase
G1 as “explicit object state helps,” and use a Δ=0 ablation if you need to
isolate *future* vs *current*.

**G2 does not change the pack.** The G2 swap feeds filter-made `[p̂, v̂]` to the
**unchanged** G1 Model B (12-D state). Oracle and filter must emit the same pack,
built by the same `interfaces.state.conditioning_vector` (plain constant-velocity
predict — no bounce-aware forecast, B never trained on one).

Still dropped: `p_hat_z`, `v_hat_z`, `sigma_*`, `valid`, `coast_time`. The filter
already fills `covariance` / `valid` in `ObjectState`; packing them needs a retrain,
so do it only **after** the G2 swap result, and only if the swap drop is ≥10 points
and retraining B on filter-made vectors did not fix it (`foresight_plan.md` §11).

## Budgets (glue, not frameworks)
| Module | Budget |
|---|---|
| Detector glue | ~50 |
| Tracker | ~100 |
| 3D lift | ~80 |
| Kalman filter | ~200 |
| Policy state append | ~50 |
| Executor buffer | ~150 |
| Reflex | ~150 |

If you need more lines, you are probably solving the wrong problem — re-read Section 10 of `foresight_plan.md`.
